ONE BINARY, SEVERAL PLUG-INS — JUCE's VST3 wrapper. Applied by cmake/PatchedWrappers.cmake to the pinned
JUCE (ORBITAMP_JUCE_TAG, 8.0.16-security) before it builds; git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line
on, so this text is not part of the patch.

JUCE registers one plug-in per binary: the factory lists one component and one controller, named and
numbered from the target's JucePlugin_ macros. With this patch a target that defines JUCE_PLUGIN_LIST_HEADER
(the name of a header on its include path) holds every plug-in that header lists in jucePluginList, and the
binary defines createPluginFilter (const juce::PluginListEntry&) instead of createPluginFilter():

  juce_PluginList.h (new)       the entry: name, four-character code, CLAP id, VST3 categories, CLAP
                                features. Plain data, no JUCE: the VST3 manifest helper compiles it.
  VST3/juce_VST3ModuleInfo.h    the factory lists a component and a controller for every entry, with the
                                class ids a build of that entry alone gives (JucePlugin_ManufacturerCode
                                and the entry's code), so moduleinfo.json lists them all too; VST2
                                replacement, compatible classes, a hand-set component id and ARA are
                                refused with an #error, being one plug-in's features.
  detail/juce_CreatePluginFilter.h   makes one entry's processor, as the single case makes its one.
  juce_audio_plugin_client_VST3.cpp  a component is made for an entry, makes that entry's processor and
                                names that entry's controller.

Without JUCE_PLUGIN_LIST_HEADER every added line is compiled out and each touched file preprocesses to its
text before the patch.

